<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Contract</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>offer &lt;player&gt;       ask what it would cost
contract &lt;player&gt;    pay, and have the player killed
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>contract Mayor
</pre>
<p>Mercenaries will kill other players for money: the Assassin on Colosseum 
Road in Midgaard is one. Stand before one and name your victim. If you 
can pay, the money is taken at once, the mercenary says "Consider them 
dead", sneaks and hides its way to the victim wherever they are, and 
attacks. Win or lose, it then vanishes in a blue cloud and returns to its 
post.
</p><p>A contract costs about 200 platinum pieces, a little more for a 
high-level victim. If you can't pay, the mercenary tells you the price. 
(The offer command quotes a much lower price at present; trust the price 
contract tells you.)
</p><p>A mercenary takes no contract on:
</p>
<ul><li>a player of level 20 or below: "Killing of newbies is not permitted!"</li>
<li>an immortal, or a monster: fight your own battles</li>
<li>yourself, or a player who is dead (a spirit), or one it can't find</li>
<li>anyone while it is still out on another job</li></ul>
<p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Assassins</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Player Killing</a>
</pre>




</div>